  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-05T08:13:40.992Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When people want to perform together, you could fix the latency by using a type of buffer. For example, if the difference in delay was 50 ms between two players, add an additional 50 ms of delay to one player and let them select a player to hear the sound without the extra 50 ms of delay. There is the flaw that the player holding the initial rhythm will still hear the second player off time, but it will sound perfectly on time to everyone else. Additionally, it would work for dancers perfectly because the musician won't be thrown off if they can't see the dance on time. If vrchat really wanted to go the extra mile, you could automate this to detect the ping difference between people and you would only need to select the player you want to play with.",
